.TH "cagebreak\-socket" "7" "2026\-06\-06" "Version 3.2.1" "Cagebreak Manual"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
\fBcagebreak\-socket\fR Cagebreak socket
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBipc\-socket\-capable\-tool $CAGEBREAK_SOCKET\fR
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The cagebreak socket is an ipc socket.\&
.PP
The socket is enabled if cagebreak is invoked with the `\-e` flag.\&
.PP
The socket accepts cagebreak commands as input (see \fBcagebreak\-config(5)\fR for more information).\&
.PP
Events are provided as output as specified in this man page.\&
.PP
.SS EVENTS
.PP
Events have a general structure as follows:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
"cg\-ipc"json object depending on the eventNULL
.fi
.RE
.PP
Here is an example of how this works using \fBonly\fR as a command sent over the socket.\&
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
only
cg\-ipc{"event_name":"fullscreen",
"tile_id":2,
"workspace":1,
"output":"eDP\-1"}
.fi
.RE
.PP
This documentation describes the trigger for the events, the keys and the data
type of the values of each event.\&
.PP
